quran[9]{c,v,t}:
  41,30,"Indeed, those who say: ‘Our Lord is Allah,’ and then remain steadfast, the angels descend upon them (saying:) ‘Do not fear, nor grieve, and rejoice with the good news of the Paradise you have been promised."
  41,31,"We are your supporters in the life of this world and the Hereafter. You shall have in it whatever your souls desire, and you shall have in it whatever you ask for,"
  41,32,"as a hospitable welcome from the Most-Forgiving, the All-Merciful (Lord).’"
  41,33,"And who is more beautiful in speech than the one who calls (others) to Allah, acts righteously and says: ‘Indeed, I am among those who submit (to Him)’?"
  41,34,"Virtue and vice cannot be equal. And repel (evil) with what is best (in conduct). (If you do so,) behold the one with whom there is enmity between you and him—he will become as though he were a sympathetic friend."
  41,35,But none is granted this (result) except those who are patient. And none is granted it except the one with a large share (of steadfastness by Allah’s Grace).
  41,36,"If an evil whisper of Satan disturbs you with intrusive thoughts, seek refuge in Allah. Indeed, He is the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing."
  41,37,"Among His signs are the night and the day, the sun and the moon. So do not prostrate to the sun or the moon, but prostrate to Allah Who created them (all) if you truly worship Him alone."
  41,38,"If they are (still) arrogant, (let them know that) those (angels) who are in the presence of your Lord glorify Him night and day, and they are never tired."
